      <offset unit="byte">0</offset>
      <records>2701</records>
      <description>Numerical shape model of N8 Proteus from data from the Voyager 2 mission. Coordinates are planetocentric, increasing to the west for planetary satellites, and to the east for (prograde) asteroids and comets, as recommended by the IAU Working Group on Cartographic Coordinates. See the data set description for details on the coordinate system. Described in Stooke (1994b). This shape model consists of a grid with points every 5 degrees in latitude and longitude, with a radius in km associated with each point. The model is planetocentric.</description>
      <record_delimiter>Carriage-Return Line-Feed</record_delimiter>
